**CVE-2021-4034 (PwnKit)** is a **heap-based buffer overflow** in **Polkit’s `pkexec`** (PolicyKit) that allows **local privilege escalation** to **root** on default Linux installations. Discovered by **Qualys Research Labs**, it affects **Polkit versions < 0x5583ca81** (v0.105 to v0.120).

---

#### **Technical Exploit Mechanics:**

##### **1. Vulnerable Code Analysis**
The flaw exists in `pkexec`’s **argument parsing**:
```c
// pkexec.c (Polkit <= 0.120)
gint main (gint argc, gchar **argv) {
  ...
  if (argc > 1)
    for (n = 1; n < argc; n++) {
      ...
      g_strdup_printf ("%s=%s", "ARGV", argv[n]); // Heap Overflow
      ...
    }
